  "caption": "Teaching schematic. Two fixed cameras observe one passive checkerboard (dashed, undirected sight lines). Each camera independently computes its own observed corner residuals and writes them to its corresponding record (solid arrows). The cameras do not communicate and the records remain separate. Positions and object sizes are schematic, not an optical calibration design.",
